Terms of Reference for the Horizon Scandal Inquiry:

1. The inquiry will establish the facts about what happened with the Horizon system and why. This includes understanding and acknowledging what went wrong and the key lessons that must be learned.
2. The inquiry will have full access to all available relevant evidence from the Post Office, Fujitsu, BEIS, and any other relevant sources.
3. The inquiry will not be prevented from monitoring individual cases, and the Horizon Compensation Advisory Board (HCAB) shall produce written reports in respect of each of their meetings.
4. The membership of HCAB will be increased to ensure that it has sufficient capacity to consider all cases and make appropriate recommendations.
5. The government will, within 28 days, seek directions under section 2(3) of the Inquiries Act 2005 to ensure that the inquiry can compel the production of evidence and the attendance of witnesses.
6. The inquiry will consider the following matters:
(a) the development, implementation, and management of the Horizon system;
(b) the role of Fujitsu in the development, implementation, and management of the Horizon system;
(c) the training and support provided to subpostmasters;
(d) the complaints and appeals process for subpostmasters;
(e) the handling of allegations of wrongdoing;
(f) the role of BEIS in overseeing the Horizon system and its impact on subpostmasters;
(g) the impact of the Horizon system on subpostmasters, their families, and communities;
(h) the adequacy of the government's response to the Horizon scandal;
(i) the steps needed to ensure that such a scandal cannot happen again.
7. The inquiry will make recommendations to the government on how to prevent such a scandal from happening again and how to support subpostmasters who have been affected.
8. The inquiry will report to the Secretary of State for BEIS, who will lay a copy of the report before Parliament.
9. The inquiry will operate in accordance with the Inquiries Act 2005 and the Inquiry Rules 2006, and will have regard to the principles of fairness,
